There are, I believe, several patches that will greatly decrease the 
difficulty of the game, or the frustration level, or whatever. You might 
try those.

If he becomes disinterested in the game, which can happen when you're 
seeing the first 10 levels over and over and over, Slash'EM may have the 
extra variety he needs. I wouldn't worry about the complication thing; 
if there are things he doesn't understand, he'll just gloss over it. 
Nethack can be played fairly easily without understanding the game 
mechanics.

Personally, I'd say you should be concerned that your kid will become 
better than you are. :)

